# API conventions

- Every public endpoint is `/v1/...`.
- Change request/response types in `packages/shared` first.
- Controllers stay thin. Validation is Zod. Business rules live in services.
- Errors use the envelope `{ error: { code, message, details?, requestId } }`.
- Auth: Bearer access JWT. Refresh tokens are hashed (SHA-256) in `Session` and rotated.
- Passwords: Argon2id only. Never log tokens, passwords, or raw verification photos.
- New tables need Prisma migrations. Do not use `prisma db push` in shared branches.
- Sensitive profile fields are never returned to other users unless a later privacy spec says so.
